cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mikha-511 or Mikha-Bench in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Mikha-511: An open-source reference implementation and degradation-stratified benchmark for flooded-road detection on public traffic-camera imagery"
abstract: >-
  Mikha-511 provides three artifacts for the flooded-road-detection problem on
  public 511 traffic-camera imagery: (1) Mikha-Aug, a deterministic library of
  five realistic 511-style degradation transforms (rain-on-lens, fog, night,
  glare, low-bitrate JPEG); (2) Mikha-Bench, a publicly released
  degradation-stratified evaluation corpus with per-image polygon water masks;
  and (3) Mikha-Ref, a laptop-runnable reference implementation combining a
  pretrained water-segmentation backbone with a temporal-persistence gate and
  calibrated confidence, intended as a reproducible baseline for the community.
type: software
